course: dictionary
lesson: 15782
title: Typographical
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Typographical is a long word, but you can break it into parts. Typo means a mistake in print or typing, and -graphical has to do with writing. So a typographical error is a mistake made when typing or printing. Use the word when you talk about books, signs or computer work.
explain: «The newspaper had a typographical error in the headline.» The sentence tells you the mistake was in the printing, not that the writers did not know the facts. Ask yourself: is the mistake about the letters on the page, or about what the words mean? If it is about the letters, typographical is the right word.
explain: Typographical can also be written as typographic. Both mean the same thing. A teacher may circle a typographical error in your story, and that is a hint to check your spelling and typing, not a sign you do not understand the story.
fact: Typographical means to do with typing or printing letters and words.
fact: A typographical error, or typo, is a mistake made when typing or printing, such as a wrong or missing letter.
fact: Typographical can also be written as typographic, and the two words mean the same.
fact: «A typographical error» tells the reader the mistake came from the typing, not from the person's knowledge.
fact: Look for context clues: if a sentence talks about a printed page, a sign or a typed word, typographical probably fits.
exercise: «The teacher circled a typographical error in my story.» What does typographical mean here? | *To do with typing or printing letters | To do with drawing pictures | To do with singing songs | To do with counting numbers
exercise: What is a typo? | *A mistake made when typing or printing, like a missing letter | A kind of cat that lives in the sea | A loud noise in the night | A big boat used for fishing
exercise: «I wnet to the shop.» Find the typographical error. | to | *wnet | the | shop
test: Another written form of typographical is which word? | *typographic | telegraphic | typical | topical
test: What does a typographical error show about the mistake? | *It was made in the typing, not because the person does not know the word | The book is very old and worn | The person cannot read at all | The writer forgot the whole story
exam: Which of these is a typographical error? | A tall tree standing in the park | A long walk to school on a sunny morning | *A missing letter in a word on a printed sign | A happy song about rain and puddles
